      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand not wanting to overreact, but I'd rather you be safe than sorry here. Intermittent chest pain with deep breaths after a long flight is still a serious warning sign — PE pain often does come and go and worsens with breathing, so \"not constant\" doesn't rule it out. Indigestion doesn't typically cause shortness of breath.\n\nI can't rule out a dangerous clot over chat, and neither can you. The only way to know is a quick evaluation — they can do an EKG, blood work, and imaging, and if it's nothing, you're home in a few hours with peace of mind. If it IS a clot, catching it now could save your life.\n\nPlease get checked tonight. It's the responsible choice, not an overreaction.",
